---
source: crates/crossfade-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: text(&out.stdout)
---
Convert a media file

Usage: crossfade convert [OPTIONS] --output <OUTPUT> <INPUT>

Arguments:
  <INPUT>  File to read: wav, flac, aiff/aifc or ogg (FLAC inside)

Options:
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          File to write; its extension picks the container: .wav, .flac, .aiff/.aif/.aifc
      --sample-format <SAMPLE_FORMAT>
          Output sample format; defaults to the input's [possible values: u8, s16, s24, s32, f32, f64]
      --codec <CODEC>
          How audio is written: copy the packets unchanged, raw pcm, or flac. Defaults to the container's own [possible values: copy, pcm, flac]
      --compression-level <COMPRESSION_LEVEL>
          FLAC effort from 0 to 8: 0 is fastest, 8 gives the smallest file
      --threads <THREADS>
          Threads for coding: auto (the default) uses the machine's cores, 1 keeps everything on one thread. The output is the same either way [default: auto]
      --force
          Replace an existing output file
      --emit-job
          Print the job as JSON and exit without touching any file
  -h, --help
          Print help
